cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the manuscript below."
title: "Perfect Aliasing in Compliant-Context Truth Probes"
abstract: >
  Compliant fitting labels cannot distinguish truth from task-prescribed action.
  Their rival AUROCs obey a complementary-label identity across 751 cell-layer
  pairs. Randomized codebooks and mixed-context fitting demonstrate linear
  recoverability in controlled tasks, with a larger fitting budget and labelled
  rival contexts. These results do not establish causal use or functional belief.
